1
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and take a step back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:24,320
Anyone short on cash, come to me.

3
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:28,980
I've got none either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:34,040
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:36,280
white clouds,

6
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:36,660
well,

7
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:40,420
somehow or other,

8
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,680
it'll work out.

9
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:46,000
You get it, right?

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,920
Got it, got it.

11
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,900
Once you understand, keep quiet

12
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,760
and follow me.

13
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,140
The worst escape on Earth

14
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,880
What time is it?

15
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,160
My head's splitting.

16
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,000
It's pitch-black. I can't see a thing.

17
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,560
Where are we? Where is this?

18
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,200
Could it be Volvo?

19
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,200
Ryotsu!

20
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,320
Don't shout so loud.

21
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,480
My head's splitting.

22
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:07,620
It's me, Honda!

23
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,380
Honda?

24
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:10,920
Thank goodness it's you, senpai.

25
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,260
This mumbling...

26
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:16,580
What's wrong?

27
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,880
Well, something fell over.

28
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,740
Wait there, I'm coming.

29
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,200
Barbar!

30
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:27,700
Damn it, I can't move in this darkness.

31
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,520
But why is there a lighter in my pocket?

32
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,300
Who's MH?

33
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,360
Hey, Sagonji!

34
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,300
Saorī!

35
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:49,460
Idiot, I'm not Saorī.

36
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:50,780
No way.

37
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:54,580
This place...

38
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,040
Not even we know.

39
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:57,760
What is this?

40
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,240
Is it a cave?

41
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:03,020
No, it's not, this wall is metal.

42
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,520
The walls are

43
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,560
50, 60 centimeters thick.

44
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,729
The ceiling is 15, 6, 7,

45
00:03:09,779 --> 00:03:12,220
8 meters high, I'd say.

46
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:16,400
Hey, with no windows or doors,
how did we even get in here?

47
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:20,440
Maybe aliens in a UFO escaped with us.

48
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:24,260
No good, there's no signal.
We can't use the phone.

49
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:28,420
Let's save the gas.
I'm turning off the light.

50
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:30,660
What's wrong?

51
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,380
I'm scared of the dark.

52
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,960
We're really stuck, aren't we.

53
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,920
Looks like we're locked in
a completely sealed room.

54
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:52,280
Is he currently out of signal range,

55
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,420
or is his phone

56
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,500
turned off?

57
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:57,380
Looks like Ryo-chan
has his phone turned off.

58
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:59,700
He's probably passed out in his room.

59
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:02,900
It was Sagonji-san's birthday yesterday,
wasn't it?

60
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:03,360
Yeah.

61
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,580
The all-guys King's Game was a real blast.

62
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:11,440
Whew, good thing I didn't go.

63
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:16,760
I left after the first place, but the senpai
went off to the second round in high spirits.

64
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,620
Then he's in no shape to work
today with that hangover, is he?

65
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,660
Let's try to remember
where we went last night.

66
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:28,640
Once we know where we are,
we should be able to find Sensō-ji.

67
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,800
Tell me anything you remember,
no matter how small.

68
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:36,680
Last night we gathered at a yakiniku place,
using Sagonji's birthday as an excuse.

69
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,900
So far, so good, right?

70
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:41,200
The green onion tongue with salt
and the kalbi were delicious.

71
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:44,400
The stone-grilled bibimbap
and the yukhoe were good too.

72
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:48,360
But above all, the dessert,
the shiratama kinako ice cream...

73
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:51,720
Enough about the food. Move on, move on.

74
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:56,240
After leaving the yakiniku place,
we bar-hopped to several spots.

75
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,640
I remember up to the third place, though.

76
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:02,780
Saori. The fourth place
was a bar called Saori.

77
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,700
And then the bar's mama...

78
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:07,700
It's Saori.

79
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:09,560
Me?

80
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,900
Thanks to that,
Sagonji got totally wasted and...

81
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:13,940
It was a nightmare.

82
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,580
What do you remember after that?

83
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,740
So we've got no clues after all.

84
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,980
Right, let's figure out how
to get out of here ourselves.

85
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:28,880
That's your specialty, isn't it.

86
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,040
Count on you, Volvo.

87
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,020
Got it.

88
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:37,260
Everyone, turn out all your belongings.

89
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,460
Well, can we make it work somehow?

90
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:51,460
No way.

91
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:55,780
Don't give up!
Use your background as an ex-Green Beret.

92
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,760
It's like something out of
a Hollywood movie, right?

93
00:05:57,760 --> 00:06:00,180
Put together some junk from around here,

94
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:05,400
and come up with some unexpected weapon,
like the guys in those movies.

95
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:09,700
Nope. Listen, Ryotsu.

96
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:15,800
In movies, they get junk that's been
pre-calculated so you can build weapons from it.

97
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:19,680
This is genuine junk, so it's impossible.

98
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:23,560
Look, being explained things
so neatly just makes me angrier.

99
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:27,820
Isn't a real pro the one who makes a great
meal from whatever's left in the fridge?

100
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:30,820
Real pros are the ones who are
picky about their ingredients.

101
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,540
What?!

102
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:34,120
If it comes to this, it's our last resort.

103
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,300
We'll use this to blow a hole in the wall.

104
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,480
Wait, you idiot, stop!

105
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:41,611
If we set this off in the dark,

106
00:06:41,661 --> 00:06:44,200
we'll all get blown to pieces along with everything else,
you idiot!

107
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:48,878
No, no!
Saori-mama's face is stuck in my head,

108
00:06:48,928 --> 00:06:51,160
and now I can't remember
my darling Saori's face!

109
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,140
Saori!

110
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:56,120
Could this possibly... be a dream?

111
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,560
Ow! It's not a dream! Ow! It's not a dream!

112
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:00,140
Yes.

113
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:02,750
I'm terribly sorry for the trouble.

114
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:06,520
Honestly,
Ryo-chan forgetting his police ID like that!

115
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,960
He got so drunk he started
taking his clothes off.

116
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:13,520
What? He hasn't come home?
Ryo-san hasn't been home since yesterday?

117
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,520
Honda-san and Sagonji-san too?

118
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,560
Ryo-chan and the others haven't come home?

119
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:22,460
It's Ryo-san, but none of the
three of them are in their rooms.

120
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,260
Are those the ones you mean?

121
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,807
So Ryo-chan and the others
left the bar around 3 a.m.,

122
00:07:28,857 --> 00:07:30,100
right?

123
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:33,353
You know,
all four of them were pretty drunk,

124
00:07:33,403 --> 00:07:35,680
so I was a little worried.

125
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,840
Volvo-san isn't reachable either, is he?

126
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,740
Didn't they say they were
going somewhere after that?

127
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:45,940
Yeah.

128
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:50,440
Right, someone suddenly
said they wanted ramen,

129
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:53,200
so I told them about a
good ramen place nearby.

130
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,880
Using up energy for
nothing will make you hungry.

131
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,360
So we just sit here quietly
and wait to become mummies?

132
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,720
If we just sit here,
someone will notice us eventually.

133
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,060
Listen carefully.

134
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:14,340
Aaaaaaah!

135
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,100
Iiiiii...

136
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:25,900
You heard the noise outside, right?
With that racket, no one will notice us.

137
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:31,320
Well, even so, that means there
are people out front, doesn't it?

138
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:46,380


139
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:48,820
Don't say that. Someone's bound
to come to rescue us eventually.

140
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:52,060
But no one even knows we're in here.

141
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,040
Four of the same business card.

142
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:03,140
Hey, who's this Mamoru Hatakeyama from
the Toyo News Agency's marketing department?

143
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:05,560
Hatakeyama.

144
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,660
I don't know him.

145
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:09,400
I don't know him either.

146
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,460
What about Sagonji?

147
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:11,420
Don't know him.

148
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,140
Mamoru Hatakeyama.

149
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:17,180
That's the MH.

150
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:22,280
This lighter apparently
belongs to this Hatakeyama guy.

151
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,880
So who exactly is this guy?

152
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:28,440
Lighter... Heegaa?

153
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,860
That's why I told you to save the gas.

154
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:39,580
Come on, pull yourself together, Honda.

155
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,120
How cool.

156
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,580
Should we do something to
take our minds off things?

157
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:49,420
Aaah... you drunk.

158
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,060
Well, nowadays,

159
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:57,820
Oh crap, we've really done it again.

160
00:09:58,380 --> 00:10:01,460
Living hell.

161
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:05,460
Shoe blisters.

162
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:11,280
Losing streak after streak...
I can't breathe.

163
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:12,720
Again

164
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,320
No good.

165
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,020
Masami.

166
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:20,760
Unsolved.

167
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:22,580
Crash.

168
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:25,620
Carpenter bee.

169
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,900
Blood and mud.

170
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,880
Prison.

171
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:35,420
Kuwabara, kuwabara...
forget it, I'm done with that.

172
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,720
That's bad luck.

173
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,620
Why is everyone only coming
up with unlucky words?

174
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,740
Instead of cheering up,
I'm getting more and more depressed.

175
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,280
Then it's the "ra" from Kuwabara, Sagonji.

176
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:48,640
You're still going with it?

177
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:52,120
It's easier to think about something,
you know.

178
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,020
Okay, let's keep it bright, bright!

179
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:56,520
It's "ra," right?

180
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,320
Lionel Richie.

181
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,720
Who's there?

182
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,780
That voice just now...

183
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:17,380
there's another one.

184
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:20,320
Listen,
don't move until we know who the enemy is.

185
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:21,220
Enemy.

186
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:24,920
They say men have seven enemies, don't they?

187
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,040
So that means that between the two of us,

188
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:29,720
there are 28 enemies in total?

189
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:32,280
Must be 28.

190
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:33,340
Right.

191
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,660
It's definitely an alien.

192
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,500
No, it's a salaryman.

193
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,520
Hey.

194
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,280
Hey.

195
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,400
Wait, could you be...

196
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,520
Hatakeyama Mamoru.

197
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:03,560
Well, I was completely out cold.

198
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:09,240
I can't hold my liquor at all, so every time I
entertain clients for work, I'm hungover the next day.

199
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,920
My head hurts.

200
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:14,880
That Hatakeyama guy knows us, right?

201
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:19,800
It's Ryo-san, Sagonji-san,
Honda-san, and Volvo-san, right?

202
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,300
Yeah, we had a great time yesterday,
didn't we?

203
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:26,660
That's right! This guy was at
the ramen shop where we got drunk.

204
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:29,500
Delicious.

205
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,160
Oyaji Ramen, getting drunk on it.

206
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:36,080
Eeh, how's Sunny-chan doing?

207
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,540
Saori!

208
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:38,800
Yes.

209
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,220
Saori!

210
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:43,520
At first I thought they were a scary bunch,

211
00:12:43,570 --> 00:12:46,920
but once we talked,
they turned out to be incredibly fun people.

212
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:48,940
Saori!

213
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:51,480
Wait, they're police officers?

214
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,800
That's right.

215
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,340
Saori!

216
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:57,340
Saori!

217
00:12:58,020 --> 00:12:59,900
Saori!

218
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:02,820
Saori!

219
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:06,220
It's been ages since I've
goofed around like that.

220
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,200
Do you remember where we are?

221
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,020
Here?

222
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,100
Where are we, exactly?

223
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:21,540
Just as I thought.

224
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:24,620
I don't remember at all
how we walked here, though.

225
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:27,180
I think I saw mountains in the distance.

226
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,040
Mountains?

227
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:30,720
Was there ever a mountain in Katsushika?

228
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:35,220
Maybe we've come a really long way.

229
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:39,320
But with drunken staggering,
how far could we possibly go?

230
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,660
This makes less and less sense.

231
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:45,340
Hatakeyama, do you remember anything else?

232
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:51,680
Otherwise, wasn't there something
important we had to do today?

233
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,880
What was it again?

234
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,580
Excuse me, what time is it now?

235
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:04,040
The watch.

236
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,220
It's half past twelve.

237
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,240
Where's the phone?

238
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,600
I'll borrow this phone.

239
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:13,980
Oh no.

240
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:17,580
Sorry, but you can't use a phone in here.

241
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:21,240
I have to go home, or I'll go home.

242
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,920
Where's the exit?

243
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:30,200
Well, we searched for it for a long time,
but it doesn't seem to be here.

244
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:30,780
Nothing.

245
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:36,640
So that means we won't be
getting out of here for a while.

246
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,640
That's a problem.

247
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:41,100
I really have to be
somewhere at one o'clock.

248
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:41,900
Where?

249
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:43,940
There's a wedding.

250
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:45,200
A wedding?

251
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,480
Whose?

252
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:48,420
Mine.

253
00:14:57,540 --> 00:15:01,540
Those four were with a young
man who looked like a salaryman,

254
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:03,300
they walked off that way, didn't they.

255
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,200
Thank you very much.

256
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,380
Chief, thanks for your hard work on patrol.

257
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,560
You're alone?

258
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:15,340
Yes, well, Reiko and Nakagawa
are out on patrol right now,

259
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:18,160
What about Ryotsu?

260
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,920
Is Ryotsu on patrol too?

261
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,400
Yes...

262
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,920
So Ryotsu is out on patrol, then.

263
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:26,620
Yes?

264
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:29,800
Your one good quality

265
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,740
is that you can never tell a lie.

266
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:32,700
Terai

267
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:36,180
Yes, yes.

268
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,460
It was last night,
in the middle of the night, you know.

269
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:41,060
My house is right behind here, you see.

270
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:44,040
With the vulgar shouting of those men,

271
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,400
my darling

272
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,420
Charis-chan was woken up.

273
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:49,760
We were terribly inconvenienced.

274
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:50,680
How about it?

275
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,620
Could they be your seniors?

276
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:53,360
Probably.

277
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:57,760
That's right,
they kept shouting some girl's name.

278
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:01,260
I think it was s-s-s...

279
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:02,320
Saori!

280
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,540
Yes, Saori!

281
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:04,660
Just as I thought.

282
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:06,980
How outrageous!

283
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,140
On top of drinking himself
senseless and skipping work,

284
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:12,460
worrying his colleagues
and causing everyone trouble,

285
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:14,180
what a good-for-nothing scoundrel!

286
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,080
Y-yes, sir.

287
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:17,340
Don't you worry, Terai.

288
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:21,480
Tell Nakagawa and Reiko to
return to their regular duties.

289
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,120
But

290
00:16:22,120 --> 00:16:26,160
I have to attend an important ceremony now,

291
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:30,540
and tell him I'll give him a
good scolding when he gets back.

292
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,040
Make sure you tell them that.

293
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,400
Y-yes, sir.

294
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:36,460
Hey, somebody help us!

295
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:37,760
Dadada!

296
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:40,520
We've tried everything already,
but nobody notices.

297
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,100
All we're doing is wasting
our strength and getting hungry.

298
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,380
But even if we just sit here doing nothing,

299
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,380
I'm sorry, Yumiko.

300
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,120
Isn't this Hatakeyama's?

301
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:11,120
This is a lighter my girlfriend gave me.

302
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,640
I see.

303
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:17,040
Don't we have a responsibility
for dragging him into this?

304
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:18,822
Even though we didn't know,

305
00:17:18,872 --> 00:17:21,380
we did drag him around the
night before his wedding.

306
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:24,460
No, I think we were told about it.

307
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,980
What, he's getting married tomorrow?

308
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:29,560
Yes, it's a big deal, you know.

309
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:32,540
So this is the lighter his
girlfriend gave him, is it?

310
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:35,340
Yes, it has my initials on it.

311
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:38,276
So, I have an early start tomorrow, so

312
00:17:38,326 --> 00:17:40,240
I'd better be heading home now.

313
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:41,420
No way!

314
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:42,560
What are you doing!

315
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,250
Since you're getting married tomorrow,

316
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:46,760
doesn't that make tonight
your last night as a bachelor?

317
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,900
And yet you're already going home!

318
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:52,640
With that attitude, you'll be under your
wife's thumb forever once you're married!

319
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:55,400
Tonight, drink with me till morning!

320
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:58,400
I'll hold on to this lighter until then!

321
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,360
W-what?!

322
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:01,340
Give it back!

323
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:02,560
Shut up!

324
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:05,220
Okay, bye-bye!

325
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:08,940
Shut up!

326
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:11,520
Then it's entirely our fault, isn't it?

327
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,012
Yeah,

328
00:18:12,062 --> 00:18:16,220
we've got to somehow get him to the wedding.

329
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,580
How?

330
00:18:18,580 --> 00:18:21,660
What are you eating?

331
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:24,640
Gum.

332
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:27,300
You ate it all, didn't you?

333
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:31,660
You! Our only food!

334
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:34,600
Don't be disappointed, I'll give it back.

335
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,020
Like I'd need it!

336
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:38,060
Come on, what are you doing!

337
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:49,380
Ryotsu

338
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:54,120
We might be able to escape, Hatakeyama!

339
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:00,660
That's the end of our clues, then.

340
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:01,740
Yeah, you're right.

341
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,060
What's wrong?

342
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:08,600
Reiko, isn't that the Chief's voice?

343
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:44,740
What a great speech, Chief!

344
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:45,300
Yeah...

345
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:49,840
They said the governor would be here,
but it doesn't look like he's arrived yet.

346
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,560
I see. That's a shame.

347
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:54,580
I really wanted you all
to hear my great speech.

348
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,700
The Chief is here too.

349
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:07,460
Hey, Kei-chan.

350
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,440
I wonder what that is.

351
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:27,580
We will now begin the unveiling ceremony.

352
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,520
Senpai, hurry!

353
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,240
Then, please go ahead.

354
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,820
Ready... go!

355
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:53,260
Okay.

356
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,900
Get down, Hatakeyama!

357
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:16,640
The Great Buddha got angry!

358
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,500
No way.

359
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,280
Why?

360
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:22,200
Couldn't calm his anger.

361
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:33,440
We did it!

362
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:35,540
We're outside! We got out!

363
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,300
Whoa! Four of them!

364
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:39,640
What is this?

365
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,540
Could this be...?

366
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,100
The Great Buddha?

367
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:54,060
How did we end up in a place like this?

368
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,860
We're on a mountain, you know.

369
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:57,500
What?!

370
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,060
Darn it, we couldn't get it off!

371
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:01,580
No way!

372
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:03,020
Give it back!

373
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:04,740
Hey, what?

374
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:06,040
My lighter!

375
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:10,580
What happened?

376
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:18,780
A mountain! Alright!
Let's climb the mountain!

377
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,720
Give me back my lighter!

378
00:22:21,760 --> 00:22:23,140
Hey! See, it's really true!

379
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:25,460
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

380
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:26,020
Okay!

381
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:28,880
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

382
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:30,200
Sweet.

383
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,440
Sweet.

384
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:31,960
Sweet.

385
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:32,580
Sweet.

386
00:22:52,180 --> 00:22:54,280
S-so that's how it was.

387
00:23:27,980 --> 00:23:29,040
How about that

388
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:31,600
Looks like we'd better
pretend we never saw this.

389
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:32,480
Yes, that's right.

390
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,840
Alright! Let's give it a go!

391
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:37,780
Let's go!

392
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:40,200
The ceremony starts in just five minutes.

393
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,940
Five minutes? That's a piece of cake!

394
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:47,000
Hey! You colossal idiot!

395
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:48,900
Hey, even if you say that...

396
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:53,820
We got locked in and nearly became Buddhas ourselves,
yabu-chaa!

397
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:57,160
It's your fault, you blasphemous fool!

398
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:01,040
Whoa, I'm sorry!

399
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:03,380
Compassionate tea farce, Kiyo

400
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:20,280
Of the rainy day after,
as if someone were calling

401
00:24:29,540 --> 00:24:34,260
The strange feeling I felt

402
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:39,540
So, on the arcade street's tiles,

403
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones.

404
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:51,480
Everyone was a child once,

405
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:53,460
but everyone forgets.

406
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,620
And the politicians with
their self-important faces...

407
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:16,380
Over there is Kameari

408
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:19,720
Well, surely it's Kameari

409
00:25:21,140 --> 00:25:24,940
Come on, everyone, to our town

410
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:26,460
Thank you

411
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:31,580
100 million yen

412
00:25:31,580 --> 00:25:34,520
Why has a 100 million
yen bonus been deposited?

413
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:36,740
Wait, even if it's a mistake

414
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:39,360
once it's in my account, it's mine

415
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:40,780
withdraw the whole amount

416
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:44,020
and pay back every penny of
the debts I've built up until now

417
00:25:44,020 --> 00:25:46,740
Next time: Bonus Scramble 6

418
00:25:46,740 --> 00:25:48,140
See you

419
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:51,000
Over there is Kameari

420
00:25:51,980 --> 00:25:54,340
Well, surely it's Kameari

421
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:59,360
Come on, everyone, to our town

422
00:26:00,460 --> 00:26:00,940
Thank you

